---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import EvidenceLabel from '../components/EvidenceLabel.astro';
import TechnicalField from '../components/TechnicalField.astro';
import { fiveGaps, missions } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Canada2080 | Capability for a changing planet"
  description="Canada2080 is a public national initiative for Canadian-controlled capability, economic sovereignty, and sustainable strategic innovation."
>
  <section class="hero shell">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Canada2080 / Public national initiative</p>
      <h1>Capability for a<br />changing planet.</h1>
      <p class="hero-deck">Canada2080 helps investors, institutions, and policy leaders build the linked capabilities required for Canadian economic sovereignty and global leadership by 2080.</p>
      <div class="action-row">
        <a class="button button-primary" href="#five-gaps">Read the problem</a>
        <a class="text-link" href="/join">Join the work <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
      <p class="provisional-note">Working tagline pending stakeholder testing.</p>
    </div>
    <TechnicalField label="2080 horizon / system field" />
  </section>

  <section class="section shell split-section" aria-labelledby="problem-title">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">The problem spine</p>
      <h2 id="problem-title">Canada has meaningful strengths. It needs stronger conversion and control.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="reading-column">
      <EvidenceLabel label="Qualified claim" />
      <p>Canada has research, talent, infrastructure, and market assets. The connected challenge is turning priority knowledge into Canadian-controlled production, learning, demand, and reinvestment.</p>
      <p>Economic sovereignty means the practical ability to make, finance, govern, repair, improve, and redirect essential capabilities from Canada while trading and collaborating internationally.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/five-gaps">Explore the Five Gaps <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="five-gaps" class="section shell gaps-section" aria-labelledby="gaps-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Francis Wang's Five Canadian Systemic Gaps</p>
        <h2 id="gaps-title">Five linked constraints on capability.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Originated in Francis Wang's 2025 DDes research proposal, <em>Foresight-Driven Innovation</em>. The gaps are a problem frame for public research and action.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="gap-list">
      {fiveGaps.map((gap) => (
        <li>
          <span class="gap-number">{gap.number}</span>
          <div><h3>{gap.title}</h3><p>{gap.summary}</p></div>
          <EvidenceLabel label={gap.evidenceClass} />
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-inverse" aria-labelledby="missions-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">A mission portfolio</p>
          <h2 id="missions-title">Regional delivery. National common services.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>Canada2080 proposes six missions to test where evidence, capital, institutions, demand, and public accountability can connect.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="mission-grid">
        {missions.map(([number, title, summary]) => (
          <li><span>{number}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{summary}</p></li>
        ))}
      </ol>
        <a class="button button-light" href="/missions">Explore the missions</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section shell split-section" aria-labelledby="climate-title">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Preparedness and managed growth</p>
      <h2 id="climate-title">Prepare capabilities before conditions demand them.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="reading-column">
      <EvidenceLabel label="Scenario" />
      <p>Under defined climate and demographic scenarios, billions of people may be exposed to less favourable climatic conditions. Exposure is distinct from displacement, migration, or movement to Canada.</p>
      <p>Canada2080 tests a preparedness approach: climate-safe housing, energy, water, services, lawful pathways, and resilient infrastructure in existing receiving regions, with rights-holder-supported regional capacity where appropriate.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section shell join-panel" aria-labelledby="join-title">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">An invitation to contribute</p>
      <h2 id="join-title">Choose one capability that Canada must make, finance, govern, repair, improve, and renew.</h2>
    </div>
    <div><p>Commit evidence, capital, institutional capacity, or policy action. Canada2080 convenes work around specific missions and accountable public value.</p>        <a class="button button-primary" href="/join">Find your role</a></div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
